Split from k237. tool_wire_format is engine-scoped (ADR 0001/0006); NousResearch's inference-api now fronts ~341 models where non-Hermes slugs take native OpenAI tools. Supporting that means a model-scoped tool_wire_format (layer-3-like, keyed on chat_model) — an ADR-level decision touching the value-object dispatch, capability registry (tools_native vs tools_hermes per model) and the manifest. Needs a design pass (llm-advisor + ADR) before any code.

2026-09-25 07:35 llm-advisor design pass (2026-09-25, code-read + 1 offline perl probe, no live calls). RECOMMEND D: per-instance, model-aware tag on NousResearch only; tool-transport flags follow the resolved tag. REJECT B (generic declarative table); C is the fallback.

KEY FACTS
1. hermes is not a dialect of the endpoint. Nous speaks OpenAI /chat/completions for every slug; hermes is a client-side way of carrying tools in the prompt. The envelope (ADR 0006, manifest dialect openai-chat) stays the same. Only the tool transport changes per model.
2. Only one engine needs it. OpenRouter / HuggingFace / Replicate / AKIOpenAI send native tools for every model; per-model "no tools" is already layer 3 (tools_native=>0). AKI native is hermes for all models (the /api/call/{model} body has no tools key), so that is endpoint-wide. vLLM / Ollama / llama.cpp tool parsing depends on how the server was launched, not on the model id, so a per-instance constructor arg fits them better than a model table. ADR 0016 rule: no framework seam until a 2nd consumer from a different parent.
3. EXISTING BUG (probed offline): tool_wire_format has an init_arg. NousResearch->new(model=>"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6", tool_wire_format=>"openai") gives fmt=openai, but capabilities stay tools_native=0, tools_hermes=1, tool_choice_named=0. Cause: HermesTools around engine_capabilities (HermesTools.pm:196) deletes the native flags no matter what the tag is. Result: the tools go out natively, but chat_f still rewrites a forced tool to json_schema, and supports() is wrong.
4. MANIFEST HAZARD (probed): clone_object copies an already-built lazy tool_wire_format. After $h->tool_wire_format has been read, clone_object($h, chat_model=>"x")->tool_wire_format still returns "hermes". Builder::_capabilities_for (Builder.pm:479) would publish stale per-model flags as soon as the tag depends on the model.
5. Per-request model override: chat_f(model=>...) passes through %extra and replaces the body model in OpenAICompatible::chat_request (the %extra comes last), but every wire decision still uses chat_model. This hole already exists for all of layer 3, 0023 and 0024. A model-scoped tag makes it worse: a Claude slug would get the hermes prompt. It is undocumented, and nothing in core, raider or knarr uses it.
6. Filed knarr k20 (high): Router _engine_cache_key = engine|url|key_env with no model. A second model on the same engine reuses the first instance, and Handler::Router then relabels the response with the model the client asked for. Every model-scoped decision (today's layer 3 and this proposal) is evaluated for the wrong model. Must be fixed before D pays off behind knarr auto_discover.
7. Siblings: knarr Request::chat_f_args gates on tools_native || tools_hermes, so it works with D as long as the flags follow the tag. Raider only renders history per the engine tag, per instance, so no change. skeid does not read either. Manifest schema: no change, because tools_native / tools_hermes per model already carry this (ADR 0029 allowlist).
8. Live (hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/integrations/nous-portal, read 2026-09-25): Hermes + 280+ models; "routing for a given model can change over time"; slugs are OpenRouter-style (anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6). Nous says Hermes 4 is "not recommended" for tool loops. UNVERIFIED: whether the Nous backend accepts native tools for Hermes-4. If it does, hermes is unnecessary on Nous. Settle with an approved live probe before step (c).

SKETCH (ADR 0031 "tool_wire_format is resolved per engine instance; tool-transport flags follow the resolved tag"; amends 0001/0002/0019)
a. Invariant: tool_wire_format is resolved ONCE per instance, from constructor arg > engine builder (may read chat_model, which is ro) > dialect default. It is never re-derived per request. Per-request model override is unsupported for model-scoped decisions: chat_f / chat_stream_realtime_f carp when $opts{model} differs from chat_model (separate small ticket, covers layers 3/0023/0024 too).
b. Role::HermesTools layer-2 rule keys on the tag, not on composition: if tool_wire_format eq "hermes", delete tools_native tool_choice_any tool_choice_named parallel_tool_use; otherwise delete tools_hermes. This fixes fact 3 by itself. Layer-3 corrections still run afterwards.
c. NousResearch::_build_tool_wire_format: hermes when chat_model =~ qr/\A(?:nousresearch\/)?(?:deep)?hermes/i, else openai. Hermes is the named exception and native is the default: 280+ native models, and an unknown new slug is far more likely native. The user override keeps working via init_arg.
d. NousResearch reasoning => 1 (Hermes system-prompt toggle) carps and is ignored when the tag is not hermes.
e. Manifest::Builder probe: add clearer _clear_tool_wire_format (Role::Tools) and call it on the probe after clone_object, both in _capabilities_for and in add_engine. Test: build the tag first, then two models (Hermes + claude slug), and assert different tools_native / tools_hermes.
f. StaticModels -> live /v1/models (the endpoint serves it per k237), with the static Hermes list kept as offline fallback. Separate ticket, only after knarr k20 (auto_discover would otherwise fan 341 slugs onto one instance).
g. Tests: request-building for both slugs (Hermes: system-prompt tools, no body tools; claude slug: body tools + named tool_choice, no synthetic rewrite); capability flags per slug; constructor override consistency (fact 3); t/78 unchanged.
Cost: roughly 30 lines in core (HermesTools rule, one builder, one clearer + Builder call, one carp) plus tests. No value-object changes, no manifest schema change, no sibling changes beyond knarr k20.

WHY NOT A: leaves bug 3 and the Builder hazard in place, and the documented escape hatch "OpenAIBase at this URL" does not work well (no default url / key env / list_models). WHY NOT B: one consumer (ADR 0016). A framework table keyed on chat_model would sit next to layer 3 but drive dispatch rather than flags, which the 0019 layer model does not cover, and it gains nothing over (c). C (a NousPortal class on openai tools, same key env) is a sound FALLBACK if the ADR discussion wants the tag strictly class-bound: zero seam change, AKI/LMStudio family precedent. Downside: users must pick the class by model, and the Hermes class still silently hermes-wraps a Claude slug. Even under C, apply (b) and (e), because they fix existing bugs.

Verdict: D is safe with the listed prerequisites (b, e, knarr k20, plus a live probe of native tools on Hermes-4 before c).

Prereqs filed: k251 (facts 3+4, steps b+e) here; knarr board k20 (router cache ignores model).

